  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">Projet Japon Bossangoa.In the Central African Republic (CAR), the number of people in need of assistance has increased across all sectors between 2022 and 2023, ranging from food security, and nutrition to WASH (water, sanitation, and hygiene), protection and GBV. In 2023, 3.4 million people (56 % of the population) need humanitarian assistance and protection, up 10 % compared to 2022. Soaring food insecurity is one of the major causes of vulnerability and distress for the population in CAR, whi</narrative>
  </description>
